{
  "headline": "FDA's shortage list shows fentanyl citrate injection current since 2012-01-01 for Hospira and Fresenius Kabi, and since 2023-12-20 for Hikma; no FDA action at a registered plant precedes the earliest posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D6", "E31", "E29", "E30"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's shortage list records fentanyl citrate injection as current for Hospira, Inc. (a Pfizer Company) with an initial posting date of 2012-01-01 and an update date of 2026-10-08.",
      "cites": ["E31"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The same list shows Fresenius Kabi USA, LLC as current with an initial posting date of 2012-01-01 and an update date of 2026-10-15.",
      "cites": ["E29"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hikma Pharmaceuticals USA, Inc. appears as current with an initial posting date of 2023-12-20 and an update date of 2026-10-14.",
      "cites": ["E30"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA's database start date is 2012-01-01, so the shortage began on or before that date and no gap is measured from it.",
      "cites": ["D6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hospira's registered plant (FEI 1021343) received OAI classifications in 2010-01-19, 2011-06-17, and 2011-08-04, all after the 2012-01-01 posting, and its most recent inspection was NAI on 2025-02-07.",
      "cites": ["E10", "E12", "E14", "E20"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hikma's registered plant (FEI 2220525) has only VAI inspections, the latest ending 2024-06-12 with a known date of 2024-12-16, and its label shows last inspection NAI 2026-05-13.",
      "cites": ["E27", "E28"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule-based best option is to transfer 74 syringes of 50 ug/mL, 1 mL from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would raise Corvale East from 5.6 days to 10 days on hand while Corvale General retains two weeks of supply.",
      "cites": ["D7"]
    }
  ]
}
